#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0581 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: None of TRTP, TRTPGy, TRTA, and TRTAGy are present and none of the character treatment variables in ADSL defined in the IG are present
#note "Only TRT1P is present: a one-digit index is no member of the TRTxxP family (xx is exactly two digits, the IG's 01-99), so count(find_vars('TRTxxP')) == 0 holds and, with none of the other 13 treatment variables present, the rule fires once for the dataset (PLAN-dynamic-column-functions review round 1, lane B L8 — pins the template's width, the narrowing the ${*} digit run would not have)."
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL type=Num
col TRT1P type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 12.5 | X
---
